**user**:
> How can I create a slider in Shiny, where the values are on a log-scale. So, I would label "$1M / yr", "$10M/yr", and "$100M /yr" along the slider, but allow people to choose values in between these. I also want there to be a paired text box, which people can also edit to set the slider.
**assistant**:
> To create a slider input on a log scale in Shiny with labeled ticks and a paired text input that can modify the slider value, you can utilize the `sliderInput()` and `textInput()` functions, along with some reactive programming to keep them in sync. Here's an example of how you can achieve this:
> 
> ```r
> library(shiny)
> 
> ui <- fluidPage(
>   titlePanel("Log Scale Slider with Paired Text Input"),
>   sidebarLayout(
>     sidebarPanel(
>       sliderInput("log_slider", "Choose Annual Income:",
>                   min = log10(1e6), max = log10(1e8), # log scale from $1M to $100M
>                   value = log10(1e7),                 # default $10M
>                   step = 0.1,
>                   pre = "$", sep = ",", 
>                   ticks = FALSE),
>       textInput("text_input", "Manual Input:", value = "$10,000,000")
>     ),
>     mainPanel(
>       textOutput("selected_value")
>     )
>   )
> )
> 
> server <- function(input, output, session) {
>   
>   # Observe changes in slider input and update text input
>   observeEvent(input$log_slider, {
>     updateTextInput(session, "text_input", 
>                     value = paste0("$", format(10^input$log_slider, big.mark = ",", scientific = FALSE)))
>   })
>   
>   # Observe changes in text input and update slider input
>   observeEvent(input$text_input, {
>     numeric_value <- as.numeric(gsub("[$,]", "", input$text_input))
>     if (!is.na(numeric_value)) {
>       updateSliderInput(session, "log_slider", 
>                         value = log10(numeric_value))
>     }
>   })
>   
>   output$selected_value <- renderText({
>     paste0("You have selected: ", input$text_input)
>   })
> }
> 
> shinyApp(ui = ui, server = server)
> ```
> 
> ### Explanation:
> 
> 1. **Log-Scale Slider:**
>     - Use `sliderInput()` with `min = log10(1e6)` and `max = log10(1e8)` to represent $1M to $100M.
>     - The `value`, `step`, and `ticks` options help configure the slider's behavior and aesthetics.
>    
> 2. **Ticks and Labels:**
>     - Although the slider doesn't show the numbers directly with tick marks, increasing `step` granularity and formatting can help users select precise intermediate values.
>     
> 3. **Paired Text Box:**
>     - Use `textInput()` to allow users to enter a specific value.
>     
> 4. **Reactivity:**
>     - Use `observeEvent()` to keep the slider and text input synchronized.
>     - When the slider changes, update the text input to reflect the slider's value converted back from log scale.
>     - When the text input changes, handle it by parsing the numeric input and updating the slider.
> 
> 5. **Output Text:**
>     - Display the formatted selected value.
> 
> This setup allows users to interact with either the slider or the text box, providing flexibility in how they input their desired value.
